<title>UK: UK 1996 barley yields highest on record - Dalgety.</title>
<headline>UK 1996 barley yields highest on record - Dalgety.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields from both this year's winter and spring barley crops are the highest on record, Britain's leading food and agribusiness group Dalgety plc said at a news conference on Thursday</p>
<p>Andrew Barnard, arable crop marketing manager for Dalgety Agriculture said the overall winter barley yield rose to 6.7 tonnes per hectare with an output of 5.08 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Spring yields reached an average of 5.7 tonnes per hectare, producing 2.9 million tonnes of barley. He gave no comparative figures for the 1995 crop.</p>
<p>Dalgety Agriculture is the agribusiness arm of Dalgety plc. -- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
